I would like to build a "task / todo manager" program.  I like the general idea of
TaskWarrior ( https://taskwarrior.org/ ), in particular I like that it can operate well at
the CLI/TUI, but in actual use I found it did't really help to keep me on task.  Part of
this is that I have tasks coming in all the time, so it's easy to get buried in work.
I'd like this all written in go.  It probably should also have an MCP interface.

Background: Right now I use just a text file to track my work, I have a list of "What I've
done" by date, usually a sentence per thing I've done, though work on a task might not
complete it.  Then below that dated log of what I've done, there's lines indicating "what
I need to do.  The file grows both ways from my "active" point, things I've done are added
as lines above where I'm at now, and things to do are added below that.  FYI: I don't need
the new system to mimic this, I'm just telling you so you can get an idea of my current
workflow.  It works ok, but I feel like there's opportunity for improving it.

For example, I might have something in my "todo" section like "Set up keycloak postgres
cluster", but then today I might add items like "Added Ansible role for postgres cluster",
"Created pgk cluster in dev", etc, and this might take several days.

Here are some of the features I'd like:  I think I'd like it to have multiple interfaces:
CLI, a TUI, and a web interface; that probably means we need a server that is where the
sqlite database exists, and the TUI and CLI and web frontends use an API to interface with
it.  I'd like the "done" items to have a date on them (it probably doesn't need time
resolution; maybe store date+time but typically only show date unless you look at detailed
view; sometimes I add a work note well after the work was done, like at night doing a
recap).  It would be nice for the "done" items to be associated with the "todo" item they
are a part of.  Sometimes items are "one-and-done", like "Run ansible against dev qt
cluster", I might just close that once I've done it without adding multiple "done
sub-records", I may want to edit the "todo" name at the point I close it ("Run ansible
against dev qt" -> "Add svc-cluster weencrypt name to certs"). In other words:
In some cases "todo" items might transition directly to a "done" item, but in other cases
I might want to add a "done" (or maybe we should call them "work"?) record when I've done
partial work on the item but am not done with it (maybe you can come up with a better name
for the "worked" records).

I may also want to add "notes" to "work" records; the "todo" or "done" record would have
a title that is a brief description, but I might want to add extra notes about that work.

I also need the ability to triage upcoming work, to order them.  In some cases I might
want to mark an task as "upcoming" with a date (or even date+time), in which case that
item should present itself on the day it's due in the triage list, or maybe in an
"upcoming" section.  I also would like a triage ability to mark a time slot throughout
today that I'd like to try to get something done; blocking out my day, but those time
blocks would be different than due dates, and any time blocked things I miss should go
back into the top of "todo" the next day for me to re-triage.  It's probably worthwhile
tracking when things get "blocked out", and when they slip.

I could imagine a singe mega "work" database record that has a description and a note and
a status and due and timeblock, and priority, and "related work" and "notes" section.

I'd also like it to be able to render a "work report" like my current work text file that
lists by day what items I have done.
